WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:02.090
The Tower of London.

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:06.820
One of the most famous towers out there, next
to The Sears Tower and The Leaning Tower of

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:07.820
Pisa.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:13.849
A place where tourists go to gawk at history,
uncomfortably large and bold ravens, and ask

00:00:13.849 --> 00:00:17.830
the timeless question “Why are the guards
called Beefeaters?”

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.160
But enough jokes, this iconic site is no laughing
matter.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:27.050
The Tower is best known for its blood-soaked
history as the site of hundreds of imprisonments

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:32.900
and executions over the years, as well as
a fair share of murders.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:38.130
Three Queens, Anne Boleyn, Jane Gray, and
Catherine Howard, lost their heads there.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:43.770
Edward V and Richard, Duke of York were found
murdered there, still only children when they

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:44.830
died.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:48.760
King Henry VI was killed during his prayers
in his private chapel.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:54.399
The list goes on and on, and the blood continues
to flow.

00:00:54.399 --> 00:00:59.110
It is no surprise that many consider the Tower
of London to be among the most haunted places

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:04.820
in the world; few locals have seen such an
intense concentration of violent, tragic death

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:05.950
and misery.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:10.260
There are reports of Queen Anne Boleyn wandering
the halls with her severed head tucked under

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:15.520
her arm, the little murdered princes frolicking
through the corridors in the dead of night,

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.910
and the Countess of Salisbury reenacting her
horrific execution, in which she was hacked

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.400
to death as she fled.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:27.330
If you’re at all enthused in British royal
history, you may know about all of these people

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.630
and their grisly ends already.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:35.350
But what you may not know about is a formerly
imprisoned man known as the Wizard Earl.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:40.770
Henry Percy, 9th Earl of Northumberland, also
known as the Wizard Earl due to his involvement

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:45.600
in the occult, was imprisoned in the Tower
of London in the late 1590s.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.000
Though he was a prisoner, he lived a relatively
comfortable life and was allowed to continue

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.750
his research and build a small library of
books and other academic materials in his

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:55.750
room.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:02:01.200
He died in November of 1632, and the secrets
of his research died with him.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.460
That is, until Martin Tower was being renovated
hundreds of years later.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:11.310
During the process of renovations to the Martin
Tower, a hidden chamber was discovered beneath

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.560
the tower’s structure.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.310
It did not appear on any official blueprints
of the building.

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:20.810
The chamber contained scattered notes and
papers, and a sturdy iron door.

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:25.760
Despite several attempts, the door could not
be opened by any ordinary means.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.660
Further investigation of the papers found
in the chamber revealed that they were research

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:34.870
notes penned by Henry Percy, who is thought
to have created the chamber and the door within

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:35.870
it.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:41.120
The notes were unusual and ominous, hinting
at a sense of otherworldly danger.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:47.890
A particularly unsettling note was an unsent
letter, from Henry Percy to famed playwright

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.440
Christopher Marlowe.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:54.510
In the letter, Percy apologizes to Marlowe
for refusing to accept his warning about building

00:02:54.510 --> 00:03:00.580
the “Janus Gate” - a significant term,
as Janus is the Roman deity that represents

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.620
beginnings, transitions, and passageways.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:11.209
The letter also references a cursed play - most
likely The Hanged King’s Tragedy, or SCP-701

00:03:11.209 --> 00:03:13.300
- which Percy begs Marlowe to destroy.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:17.970
He ends the letter by saying that he has sealed
the gate, permitting only the enlightened

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:22.090
to enter it so that they might perhaps see
what Percy could not.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:27.349
The letter concludes: “Damn that Metropolis
of Blood, that terrible Realm and its ancient

00:03:27.349 --> 00:03:28.890
countless Crimes.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:35.790
Consign thy Play to the Fire, deny thy vile
Patron, and aroint thee from this Madness.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:38.580
We would fain welcome thee back into the Night.”

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:43.580
More troubling, perhaps, than the contents
of the letter itself is the date it was to

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:46.519
be sent: May 30, 1593.

00:03:46.519 --> 00:03:50.909
The day before Marlowe was murdered.

00:03:50.909 --> 00:03:55.299
Suspecting the presence of an anomalous artifact
the Janus Gate referenced in Percy’s notes

00:03:55.299 --> 00:04:00.769
and letters, the Crown hurriedly contacted
the SCP Foundation and requested they perform

00:04:00.769 --> 00:04:02.940
a thorough investigation.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:09.800
What they found was unlike anything the Foundation
has ever encountered, before or since.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:14.880
Henry Percy was speaking truthfully in his
letter, he did seal off the door in his secret

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:15.880
chamber.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:20.419
The only way to open it is to complete a series
of alchemical instructions, similar to those

00:04:20.419 --> 00:04:23.169
used in the creation of a Philosopher’s
Stone.

00:04:23.169 --> 00:04:28.590
A resident Alchemy expert at the Foundation
assisted in finding the solution, and, for

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:33.770
better or for worse, the Janus Gate was unlocked
for observation.

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:41.419
Beyond the gate lies a city, known as SCP-2264-B.
The city is extradimensional, matching no

00:04:41.419 --> 00:04:45.479
known location on earth or anywhere else.

00:04:45.479 --> 00:04:49.949
Upon entering the city, the smell of dried
flowers and old books greets you.

00:04:49.949 --> 00:04:55.599
You glance up at the sky to find it an eerie
yellow, spotted with infinite glittering black

00:04:55.599 --> 00:04:56.599
stars.

00:04:56.599 --> 00:05:00.469
If you look down at yourself, you will find
that your clothes have disappeared, replaced

00:05:00.469 --> 00:05:03.849
with attire that would not be out of place
at a Masquerade ball.

00:05:03.849 --> 00:05:08.699
Your face is adorned with a Venetian mask
that you cannot remove, no matter how hard

00:05:08.699 --> 00:05:13.009
you try, until you have left this strange
world and passed back through the gate.

00:05:13.009 --> 00:05:17.800
If you pause to take in the sights of the
city around you, you will find buildings,

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:24.749
carved from one single undetermined material,
all in black, white, yellow, or red.

00:05:24.749 --> 00:05:27.470
These are the only colors present in the city.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:32.999
In the distance, a viscous black ocean laps
at the shore on all sides.

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:37.180
Though the ominous black liquid in said ocean
is anything but water.

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:42.301
The city, though it has been proven to exist
in a corporeal state, has the quality of a

00:05:42.301 --> 00:05:43.839
lucid dream.

00:05:43.839 --> 00:05:48.719
Operatives inside of it report difficulty
concentrating, citing a feeling of hypnagogic

00:05:48.719 --> 00:05:54.249
malaise, inability to control their impulses,
and trouble describing what they saw and did

00:05:54.249 --> 00:05:58.029
inside of the city once they have returned
to the regular world.

00:05:58.029 --> 00:06:03.719
The dimension seems to run on dream logic,
best described in the movie Inception - not

00:06:03.719 --> 00:06:09.009
everything makes sense, and transitions between
place and time seem muddy to say the least.

00:06:09.009 --> 00:06:13.860
After several expeditions that failed to return
conclusive, coherent observations about the

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:17.009
city’s nature, another exploration was planned.

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:22.770
Chosen for his experience with altered states,
mainly lucid dreaming and hallucinogenic drugs,

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:27.430
Dr. Calixto Navaez was selected to lead this
exploration.

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:34.319
Upon entering SCP-2264-B for his first exploration,
most of Dr. Navaez’s colleagues split off

00:06:34.319 --> 00:06:37.819
from him to join in the decadent celebrations
in the palace.

00:06:37.819 --> 00:06:42.860
He resisted this temptation, though of course
he considered it for a moment, and continued

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.319
on with his investigation of the city.

00:06:45.319 --> 00:06:49.999
He made several significant discoveries over
the course of this first expedition, which

00:06:49.999 --> 00:06:53.399
informed the Foundation’s perspective on
the city going forward.

00:06:53.399 --> 00:06:58.189
First, he realized that the city somehow universally
translates language.

00:06:58.189 --> 00:07:02.389
No matter what a person’s native tongue,
they will hear the inhabitants of the city

00:07:02.389 --> 00:07:03.840
speaking in it.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:08.080
Some of Dr. Navaez’s colleagues heard the
citizens speaking English, while he heard

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:10.490
them speaking in his native Spanish.

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:14.319
It is unclear how this instantaneous translation
is accomplished.

00:07:14.319 --> 00:07:19.889
Second, he learned the name of the city: Alagadda,
a city-state bordering something referred

00:07:19.889 --> 00:07:22.270
to only as the Nevermeant.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:27.550
To provide a little context and clarification,
the city of Alagadda is a nexus point for

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:30.229
a whole multi-verse of hedonists.

00:07:30.229 --> 00:07:35.499
Countless entities from every conceivable
dimension turn up here to sample its legendary

00:07:35.499 --> 00:07:36.499
pleasures.

00:07:36.499 --> 00:07:40.610
Think of it almost like a multidimensional
Cancun during Spring Break.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:44.770
He was given this information by a foreign
scholar known as the Wandsman of Kul-Manas,

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:48.159
a robed creature in a birdlike mask.

00:07:48.159 --> 00:07:52.429
The Wandsman was also able to provide some
insight into the political power structure

00:07:52.429 --> 00:07:57.869
of Alagadda, providing Dr. Navaez with his
third piece of critical new information.

00:07:57.869 --> 00:08:03.729
The city is overseen by four Masked Lords:
The Black Lord, Wearer of the Anguished Mask,

00:08:03.729 --> 00:08:09.629
The White Lord, Wearer of the Diligent Mask,
The Yellow Lord, Wearer of the Odious Mask,

00:08:09.629 --> 00:08:13.279
and The Red Lord, Wearer of the Mirthful Mask.

00:08:13.279 --> 00:08:18.209
These powerful entities act as advisors to
the city’s mighty King, who many of the

00:08:18.209 --> 00:08:21.020
travelers in the city sought a favor from.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:25.690
The Wandsman warned about each of these Lords,
stating that, in spite of their different

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.949
names, they are all equally dangerous.

00:08:28.949 --> 00:08:32.769
They also warned against interacting with
The Ambassador of Alagadda.

00:08:32.769 --> 00:08:37.000
After this illuminating conversation, Dr.
Navaez gathered the rest of his colleagues

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.339
and returned to the real world.

00:08:39.339 --> 00:08:44.060
On his second expedition into Alagadda, Dr.
Navaez immediately sought out the Wandsman

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:45.360
of Kul-Manas.

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:50.149
The Wandsman expressed concern for Dr. Navaez
and his team, warning them: “The Ambassador

00:08:50.149 --> 00:08:54.630
of Alagadda will soon return from Adytum and
only the mad shall remain.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:59.060
I suggest you leave posthaste, for I intend
the same.”

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:03.759
When pressed on the subject of Adytum, the
Wandsman explained that it is “A terrible

00:09:03.759 --> 00:09:06.079
city, filled with equally terrible people.

00:09:06.079 --> 00:09:11.910
It is said that the Grand Karcist of Adytum
serves the designs of an elder being, a horror

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:15.949
thought to rival even the Hanged King of Alagadda.”

00:09:15.949 --> 00:09:21.329
Before Dr. Navaez could gather any more answers,
the Wandsman stopped, becoming clearly frightened,

00:09:21.329 --> 00:09:24.800
and said: “I sense the Ambassador of Alagadda
has returned.

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:28.550
I take my leave of this place and I suggest
you do the same.

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:30.670
Flee; do not delay.”

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:33.800
The Wandsman promptly exited through the nearest
door.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:38.610
Following Dr. Navaez’s expeditions, the
Foundation appointed a task force of agents

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:44.180
trained in hand-to-hand combat and Counter
Occult strategies to go back into Alagadda.

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:49.699
The task force, nicknamed the Abyss Gazers,
was to seek out the King and Ambassador of

00:09:49.699 --> 00:09:54.259
Alagadda and determine the level of threat
they might pose to humanity.

00:09:54.259 --> 00:10:01.529
Twelve agents were sent in, and only one,
Agent Alexander Papadopoulos, came back alive.

00:10:01.529 --> 00:10:05.379
The other eleven are presumed dead or lost
forever.

00:10:05.379 --> 00:10:10.170
Agent Papadopoulos was found unconscious and
in critical condition outside the entrance

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:11.350
to Alagadda.

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:16.620
A physical exam was conducted, revealing broken
bones throughout his entire body as well as

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:18.750
severe internal bleeding.

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:22.750
He was in the hospital for three weeks before
the Foundation determined him healthy enough

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:24.350
for an interview.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:29.060
The interview was conducted by Dr. Laxmi Narang
and allowed the Foundation to get a sense

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:34.899
of what Agent Papadopoulos witnessed inside
the city, and what happened to the other eleven

00:10:34.899 --> 00:10:36.310
team members.

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:40.920
The team managed to locate the palace, struggling
with the dreamlike effect of the city on the

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:46.029
mind, and the lack of ability to determine
how much time had passed while they were there.

00:10:46.029 --> 00:10:51.399
As the group descended deeper into the palace,
it became more convoluted and labyrinthine.

00:10:51.399 --> 00:10:56.300
They spent most of their time descending a
staircase, traveling deeper and deeper.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:11:01.120
When they reached the bottom of the staircase,
suddenly they were outside the palace again,

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:03.490
as if they never went inside.

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:06.779
Except, everything was a little bit different.

00:11:06.779 --> 00:11:08.730
Wrong, somehow.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:13.470
The world looked dark and drained of color,
bathed in hazy gray light.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:18.089
There were no people to be seen, and the buildings
looked run down and abandoned.

00:11:18.089 --> 00:11:23.269
They walked back into the palace from this
strange new location and began to hear whispering.

00:11:23.269 --> 00:11:27.459
Not just in their ears, but in their very
minds.

00:11:27.459 --> 00:11:29.899
The Ambassador of Alagadda had found them.

00:11:29.899 --> 00:11:38.009
It appeared before them, a tall thin dark
figure with no face, no mouth, no eyes.

00:11:38.009 --> 00:11:44.030
Somehow it spoke, in a language none of the
team could understand, and it laughed.

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:49.430
As it watched, unable to control themselves,
the team began to tear each other apart.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:56.449
Flesh ripped, organs collapsed, bones shattered,
and none of them could stop themselves until

00:11:56.449 --> 00:11:59.930
Agent Papadopoulos was the only one left alive.

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:05.879
He was not left alive by mistake, the Ambassador
left him living in order to pass on the message

00:12:05.879 --> 00:12:07.769
of its existence.

00:12:07.769 --> 00:12:12.459
It dragged his limp body into the chambers
of the king and forced him to look upon its

00:12:12.459 --> 00:12:14.110
twisted form.

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:18.290
His exact terrifying words of the account
paint a gruesome picture:

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:25.749
“Eventually we stopped and it lifted me
into the air, held me up before the throne.

00:12:25.749 --> 00:12:29.390
There I saw the King.

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:36.269
It was anchored in place, hallowed bonds around
its corpse-like hands and throat - its face

00:12:36.269 --> 00:12:38.589
hidden beneath a veil.

00:12:38.589 --> 00:12:44.949
Impish creatures crawled all over it, caressing
its twitching body as if intending comfort

00:12:44.949 --> 00:12:49.269
while others pulled the tethers even tighter.

00:12:49.269 --> 00:12:54.569
The King trembled and quivered and I saw pale
tendrils slither in and out of its tattered

00:12:54.569 --> 00:12:55.569
robes.

00:12:55.569 --> 00:12:59.089
I looked on as the veil was lifted…”

00:12:59.089 --> 00:13:03.350
At this point in his interview, the Agent
became inconsolable.

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:08.570
He begged to be killed, a request which was
denied.

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:12.560
Before the interview ended, the Agent said:
“A god shaped hole.

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:16.199
The barren desolation of a fallen and failed
creation.

00:13:16.199 --> 00:13:20.170
You see the light of long-dead stars.

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:28.329
Your existence is nothing but an echo of a
dying god's screams.

00:13:28.329 --> 00:13:29.569
The unseen converges.

00:13:29.569 --> 00:13:30.569
Surrounds you.

00:13:30.569 --> 00:13:33.420
And it tightens like a noose.”

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:38.339
After the interview, Agent Papadopoulos refused
food and water and repeatedly requested to

00:13:38.339 --> 00:13:39.870
be terminated.

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:45.660
This request was denied every time, and he
was given a feeding tube for nutrients.

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:50.899
After the revelations in the Papadopoulos
interview, the Foundation suspended all research

00:13:50.899 --> 00:13:53.199
expeditions into Alagadda.

00:13:53.199 --> 00:13:59.040
It is difficult to hide SCP-2264 from the
public, due to the public nature of the building

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:00.999
the gateway is located in.

00:14:00.999 --> 00:14:05.470
Because the Tower of London cannot be shut
off to the public, the Foundation has focused

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:09.699
on hiding the gateway from anyone who might
accidentally stumble upon it.

00:14:09.699 --> 00:14:14.130
The government of the United Kingdom and the
Foundation worked together to build a secret

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:20.079
passage to SCP-2264, accessible only to authorized
personnel.

00:14:20.079 --> 00:14:23.220
The original entrance has been walled off.

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:29.449
Meanwhile, beyond the gate, Alagadda continues
in its strange, twisted ways.

00:14:29.449 --> 00:14:34.319
We do not know what the Ambassador wants,
or the nature of the other beings lurking

00:14:34.319 --> 00:14:39.930
within the city walls, but we can only hope
that they never find their way through the

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:41.740
gate to us.

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:48.730
Now go check out “SCP-261 - Pan-Dimensional
Vending Machine” and “SCP-001 - The Spiral

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:51.350
Path” for more extradimensional oddities!

